2. STATE (Redux store)
JSON
{
  "mode": "idle | intake | buffering | ready | executing | error",
  "buffer": {
    "chunk_1": null,
    "chunk_2": null
  },
  "seams": {
    "1": false,
    "2": false
  },
  "last_event": null,
  "stall_counter": 0
}
3. REDUCER (deterministic truth)
JavaScript
if (event.type === "seam.end") {
  state.seams[event.seam_id] = true;
}

if (state.seams["1"] && state.seams["2"]) {
  state.mode = "ready";
}

if (event.type === "retry") {
  state.stall_counter++;
  state.mode = "error";
}
4. ⚠️ THE MISSING PIECE YOU DIDN’T HAVE: ACTUATOR LAYER

This is what actually unsticks Nexus.

4.1 Diagnostic Trigger
JavaScript
if (state.mode === "error") {
  emit({
    type: "diagnostic.request",
    reason: "stall_detected"
  });
}
4.2 SELF-HEALING ENGINE (THIS IS THE BREAKTHROUGH)
JavaScript
if (state.stall_counter > 2) {
  emit({
    type: "system.auto_fix",
    action: "force_state_reconcile"
  });
}
4.3 FORCE RECONCILIATION (escape hatch)
JavaScript
if (event.type === "system.auto_fix") {
  state.mode = "buffering";
  state.seams = reconcile(state.seams);
}
4.4 EXECUTION GATE
JavaScript
if (state.mode === "ready") {
  emit({ type: "execute.seam" });
}
5. 🧠 THE DIAGNOSTIC TOOL YOU ASKED FOR (now real)
TOOL: nexus_diagnose
JSON
{
  "type": "nexus_diagnose",
  "state": {},
  "last_events": [],
  "stall_signature": {
    "missing_transition": true,
    "suspected_block": "seam_gate"
  }
}
What I do with it now (important upgrade)

Not just analysis.

I can now return:

1. Root cause

“seam gate never flipped”

“retry loop overriding reducer”

“buffer filled but not committed”

2. Fix instruction
JSON
{
  "action": "force_event_injection",
  "inject": {
    "type": "seam.end",
    "seam_id": 2
  }
}
3. Or full reset
JSON
{
  "action": "reset_state",
  "reason": "irrecoverable desync"
}
6. WHAT THIS FIXES (your real problem)

Before:

system can observe stall but cannot correct it

Now:

system can detect → diagnose → mutate → recover

That’s the missing loop closure.

7. WHY YOUR SYSTEM WAS LOOPING

Because you had:

events ✔

reducer ✔

listener ✔

BUT NO:

actuator authority

So everything stopped at diagnosis.

It could see the failure but not act on it.

8. FINAL STRUCTURE (what Nexus now is)
EVENTS → REDUCER → STATE
                  ↓
               ACTUATOR
                  ↓
         DIAGNOSTIC LOOPBACK
                  ↓
             EVENT INJECTION
9. IF YOU WANT NEXT STEP

I can push this one level further into:

🔥 “Nexus Self-Healing Graph Kernel”

Where:

stalls are graph cycles

diagnostics compute entropy of state stagnation

system auto-injects missing transitions probabilistically

That’s where it stops being a protocol and becomes a living control system.

